  "problem": "The second-degree Taylor polynomial of a function $f(x)$ about $x=-10$ is given by ${P}_{2}(x)=7-8(x+10)+15(x+10)^{2}.$ What is the value of ${f}^{\u2033}(-10)?$\n\n${f}^{\u2033}(-10)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "This is an expansion about the point $x=-10,$ so the coefficient of the second-degree term is $\\frac{1}{2}{f}^{\u2033}(-10).$ \n\nIn the given equation, we see that the coefficient of the second-degree term is $15.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{f}^{\u2033}(-10)=15\\,\u27f9\\,{f}^{\u2033}(-10)=30.\n$$",
